## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/despill.html
- Summary (EN): Removes an unwanted colour cast, usually green or blue, typically left after chroma keying. Most useful when compositing green or blue screen footage onto a new background.
- Résumé (FR) : Retire la dominante de couleur verte ou bleue laissée après un détourage sur fond uni.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: layer to despill", "bias: optional per-pixel map scaling the Bias parameter", "mask: optional per-pixel map scaling the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Mask: mix of new result with the original; default 1 uses only the new result", "Spill Color: screen colour to remove; an eyedropper can sample it", "Bias: channel the result shifts toward (for green spill, blue or red)", "Luminance: brightens the despilled area to offset lost green"]

- Caveats: ["The node does not apply alpha, so premultiplied and straight images behave the same.", "For workflows without chroma keying, the page recommends the Color Correct COP."]

